"Questors are never offered transformative classes."
"Early Questors kept trying for two classes until they succeeded."
"In his first week Nathan Lark chose Antimagic Brawler at level 15."
"Later Nathan held Void of Magic (Deepened Stamina) and Spellslayer (Regenerative Focus)."
"Years later he held End of Magic, with Bottomless Stamina, and the assassin class Spellslayer."
"Years later Spellslayer reached 729 and offered Death of Legends, Veilpiercer, Stalker of Horizons."
"Death of Legends is for one who killed legendary foes; it lets them face foes built to counter them."
"Stalker of Horizons is for one who travelled far to kill; it is at heart a stealth class."
"Veilpiercer is for one who can pierce magical barriers; it deepens Aether and wizardry use."
"Nathan took Death of Legends; Spellslayer 729 became Death of Legends 763, Focus max 7390 to 7730."
"Aarl's 729 offers: Duelbound, Impenetrable Aegis, Master of Adamant, Relicmaster, Slayer of Giants."
"Duelbound improves dueling; Impenetrable Aegis protects teammates; Master of Adamant, armor."
"Relicmaster boosts every magic item used and bypasses curses and item restrictions."
"Slayer of Giants inherits the lost strength and majesty of the giants; it suits city founders."
"Aarl took Relicmaster, letting him use nearly any item and identify items by touch."
"Sarah's 729 offers: Slayer of Giants, Unseen Death, Edge of the Horizon, Line-Ender."
"Unseen Death is stealth, Line-Ender power; Edge of the Horizon keeps sight clear at any range."
"Sarah took Edge of the Horizon, which Questors skip because it is weak in duels."
"Slayer of Giants gave Aarl strength but would have given Sarah motion."
"Stella's 729 offers: Heir of Wizardry, Mage of Destruction, Mana Incarnate, Citybreaker."
"Mage of Destruction favors wide-area effects; Citybreaker breaks a city's hardened defenses."
"Heir of Wizardry lets its holder imbue wizardry into all magic; Stella took it."
"Mana Incarnate turns the body into mana: bigger spells, but vulnerable to wizards."
"Khachi's 729 offers: Prophet Ascendent, Hand of Resurrection, Voice of the Purifying Flame,"
"...Light of Judgement, Saint of the Last Light and Nascent Divine."
"Nascent Divine fosters worship and Faith, the most direct path to apotheosis."
"Prophet Ascendent gives preaching skills and hints at a later option of Ascendency."
"Hand of Resurrection heals and revives the recently dead; Saint of the Last Light, protection."
"Voice of the Purifying Flame: blessings and fire combat; Light of Judgement: light that hurts foes."
"Khachi's earlier class was Shield of Hope; he took Light of Judgement and gained a halo."
"Aarl's and Stella's 729 choices upgraded every class skill, owing to a Grand Dungeon cleared."
"Sarya holds thief and messenger classes, whose skills work only while enemies don't know her."
"Years later Kamus claimed he would sunder his own class to learn Nathan's Insights."
"Years later the Heirs swore on a Seal: May my class be stripped from me if I forswear."
